## Features added from other hacks

Take the mechanism, not the stack. MindPad (HackPrinceton Fall 2025, Best Overall and Amazon Practical AI), Asclepius (a measured privacy proxy), and Lume (Fall 2025 education track: show the exact step, in speech) are the sources. Discer.io contributes only the "try a smaller problem" beat. Cortex contributes only "search the professor's own notes."

Build these in M3, after the core loop is real:

- A canary string stored with the answer key. It must never reach a student-facing body. This is Asclepius's verbatim check, aimed at our key.
- Fail closed. If the guard's JSON fails or the provider errors, the student does not see the draft. Asclepius leaked because a parse error fell through to the weak path.
- Pass rates reported by attack class, not as one comforting number.
- A level-3 related-problem card, separate from the chat bubble, so the demo is not a plain chat box. MindPad's canvas, cut down to one card.
- Typed-work highlight: mark the line that went wrong and do not rewrite it. This is Lume's "show where," and it is the fallback when the photo circle is not reliable.
- Snap-your-work: a photo in, the wrong step and a normalized box out, a red ellipse on screen. 501 until it works. Go or no-go Saturday 2 PM.
- Level-2 citation by searching the professor's pasted notes. Keyword match is enough. No new search service.
- Flashcards for that student's weakest concept, drawn from the notes, with no solution lines. MindPad's revise loop, without the answer.
- A pasted-notes field on professor setup. A PDF upload only after paste works.
- Accessibility of the two screens: contrast, focus order, and usable at 200% zoom. No camera and no gesture control.

Do not build these, even though the source projects have them: hand tracking, MediaPipe, a custom vision model, emotion or attention tracking, a shared student canvas, LMS import, differential privacy, a HIPAA stripper, clinical-trial IP detection, a Python or FastAPI backend, and LangChain deepagents. Voice is not part of M1–M3. Add voice only if the core demo already works and only if someone is actually entering the Photon voice prize.

